      "description": "Assistant Professor of Kinesiology » Rockford University Apply Now Contact Us Contact Us About Newsroom Give Library my.rockford.edu Search Mobile Navigation Academics PROGRAMS Academics Colleges and Deans Majors and Minors Undergraduate Degrees Academic Departments Professional & Extended Learning RU Online Graduate Programs Puri School of Business English Language Institute (ESL) Study Abroad Early Scholars Student Support Programming RESOURCES & SUPPORT Library Academic Affairs and Provost Academic Integrity Policy Registrar Transcript Request The HUB: Academic Coaching & Testing Services Catalog and Resources Calendars and Schedules Writing Center Spirit Shop Online Bookstore ROCKFORD DIFFERENCE Why Rockford University Community-Based Learning Phi Beta Kappa (PBK) Learning Expectations Accreditations Admission INFORMATION FOR First Year Undergraduate Transfer International Student Admitted Undergraduate RU Online Graduate Programs TUITION & FINANCIAL AID Rockford Promise Financial Aid and Scholarships Financial Aid: Step by Step Guide Tuition and Fees First-Year Student Calculator Transfer Student Calculator CONNECT Request More Information Visit and Tour Campus Apply to Rockford University Campus & Community FOR STUDENTS Campus & Community Career Development Commencement First-Year Experience Residence Life Student Activities Student Administrative Services Student Success Student Life CAMPUS SERVICES Campus Map Spirit Shop Box Offices Business Office Dining Services Disability Services IT: Information Technology Marketing & Communications Lang Wellness Center Dept of Public Safety Scheduling Services and Rentals Community President’s Office About Rockford University Calendar of Events Compliance and Title IX Global Affairs Human Resources and Employment Jane Addams Center See Something Say Something Behavioral Alert Business Summit Arts & Lectures LOCATIONS & RESOURCES Art Gallery Box Offices Theatres EVENTS & PERFORMANCES Arts & Lectures Forum Series Music Ensembles Performing Arts Season Athletics MEN’S SPORTS Baseball Basketball Cross Country Football Soccer Volleyball WOMEN’S SPORTS Basketball Cross Country Golf Soccer Softball Volleyball Flag Football Bowling RESOURCES & FAN ZONE Rockford Regents Alumni STAY IN TOUCH Alumni Alumni Association Contact Us Alumni Awards Transcript & Diploma Request ENGAGE Catalyst FOPA WRCR Golf Playday Day of Giving Homecoming Weekend Charles M. DeWild Hall Of Fame GIVE BACK Gala Alumni Referral Scholarship The Annual Fund Legacy Giving Ways to Give Campus News Rockford.edu / News Assistant Professor of Kinesiology 10/21/2026 4:02 pm Rockford University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track or teaching-track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Kinesiology. We are seeking a student-centered educator with expertise in Kinesiology, Physical Education pedagogy, Exercise Science, and/or Sport Management to contribute to our growing undergraduate and graduate programs. The successful candidate will demonstrate excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service, and will be committed to mentoring students pursuing careers in physical education, exercise science, sport management, and related fields. This position offers access to modern facilities and advanced lab equipment, and the opportunity to collaborate across disciplines in a vibrant academic community. The role includes teaching opportunities in Rockford University’s Master of Science in Exercise Physiology and/or Master of Arts in Sport Management and Leadership programs. Primary Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Biomechanics, Teaching Fitness and Conditioning, Exercise Physiology, Introduction to Exercise Science, and possibly Sport Management (e.g., Sport Marketing, Finance, Analytics, Esports, Sport Law, Event Management), and Pedagogy (e.g., Health Education, Methods of Physical Education). Supervise student internships, research projects, and lab activities using equipment. Mentor students in the BS in Exercise Science, Sport Management or Teaching track and MSEP and MASML programs. Develop curriculum, recruit students, and participate in academic advising. Maintain an active research agenda with scholarly output and potential for external funding (for tenure-track position; not required for teaching-track position). Engage in university service, professional organizations, and community outreach. Demonstrate a willingness to engage in community-based learning (CBL), linking classroom instruction to the Rockford community through experiential learning. Qualifications Required: Earned doctorate in Kinesiology, Sport Management, Exercise Science, or a closely related field (ABD considered). University-level teaching experience. Strong communication, collaboration, and organizational skills. Preferred: Professional certifications (e.g., CSCS, ACSM, ACE, ATC, CHES, CPRP). Experience with online, hybrid, and face-to-face instruction. Industry experience and connections in sport or health-related fields. Evidence of scholarly productivity (for tenure-track position; not required for teaching-track position). Active involvement in professional organizations. Experience with exercise science lab equipment and student mentorship. To apply: Review of applications will begin on immediately and continue until the position is filled. Faculty contracts are 9 months, paid over 12 months. This Tenure-track opportunity offers an annual salary of $50,000-$53,000. Please submit via a single .pdf to HumanResources@rockford.edu : Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Research statement outlining current and future research plans List of three professional references Transcripts (original upon hire) Our Benefits: Supporting You Every Step of the Way We believe in taking care of our employees, which is why we offer a competitive benefits package that goes above and beyond. Here’s how we support your health, happiness, and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage: Medical, dental, and vision insurance to ensure you and your family stay healthy. Savings for Health & Dependent Care: Flexible savings options to manage healthcare and dependent care costs. Financial Protection: Life, AD&D, and disability insurance for peace of mind when life throws you a curveball. Retirement Security: 403(b) plan with employer contributions to help you build a secure future. Personal Support: Access to our Employee Assistance Program, offering resources for both personal and professional needs. Education Benefits: Tuition remission for full-time and part-time employees, their spouses, and dependents. We offer tuition remission both at Rockford University and other partnering colleges through a tuition exchange. At Rockford University we are committed to the principle of diversity, equity and inclusion as it relates to building a well-rounded workforce and community. We are especially interested in candidates who through their professional experience bring contributions to diversity and excellence in the work they do. Return to Previous Page ROCKFORD UNIVERSITY 5050 East State Street Rockford IL 61108 815.226.4000 Faculty & Staff Directory Campus Map & Directions Virtual Tour - Visit Campus Today Library Majors and Minors my.rockford.edu Online Interactive Academic Catalog Employment Opportunities Lang Wellness Center Compliance and Title IX Emergency Information Give News Event Calendar About Rockford University President’s Office Privacy Policy IBHE Feedback Scheduling Services and Rentals Copyright © 2026 Rockford University, all rights reserved"
